+## Group Chats
+
+Without `group_trigger` the bot answers every message in a group, except messages that start with another bot's or an unknown `/command`. To narrow that:
+
+- `mention_only: true` answers only messages that mention the bot (`@yourbot`) and the bot's own commands.
+- `prefixes: ["!bot"]` answers only messages that start with a prefix, and mentions.
+
+A bare `/command` counts as addressed to the bot only when it is one of the bot's own commands, so `/print` meant for another bot in the group is not answered. `/command@yourbot` is always addressed to it.
+
+### Deciding by a decision model
+
+When several people talk in the group, a model that only judges "is this message addressed to the bot?" can replace `mention_only`/`prefixes`. It is an [OpenRouter Decisions](https://openrouter.ai/docs) model such as `typesafe/jev-1.14`: it returns a probability and generates no text.
+
+```json
+{
+  "channel_list": {
+    "telegram": {
+      "group_trigger": {
+        "decision": {
+          "model": "typesafe/jev-1.14",
+          "min_confidence": 0.5,
+          "timeout_ms": 3000,
+          "proxy": "http://127.0.0.1:7890",
+          "bot_description": "assistant of a ceramics studio: records expenses, answers about glazes",
+          "chat_description": "Telegram group of the studio staff. Other bots live in it too; slash commands without @yourbot are for them."
+        }
+      }
+    }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+The API key is a secret and lives in `.security.yml` next to `config.json`:
+
+```yaml
+channel_list:
+  telegram:
+    group_trigger:
+      decision:
+        api_key: "sk-or-..."
+```
+
+| Field            | Description                                                                                         |
+| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| model            | Decision model. The decision is enabled when both `model` and `api_key` are set                     |
+| min_confidence   | The bot answers when the probability is at least this. Defaults to 0.5                              |
+| timeout_ms       | Time limit of one decision request. Defaults to 3000                                                |
+| proxy            | HTTP proxy URL for OpenRouter (it refuses some regions); empty uses the environment proxy           |
+| bot_description  | What the bot does, shown to the model                                                               |
+| chat_description | What the chat is and which other bots live in it, shown to the model                                |
+
+What the model sees for each message: the sender and text, the message it replies to and whether that is the bot's, the last 8 messages of the chat from the past hour (including the bot's own), and the bot's last message.
+
+- A message that mentions the bot, `/command@yourbot` and the bot's own commands are answered without asking the model.
+- A message that starts with another bot's or an unknown `/command` is ignored without asking the model.
+- If the request fails or times out, the message is ignored and a warning with the error is logged. If `model` is set without `api_key`, a warning is logged at startup and the `mention_only`/`prefixes` rules apply.
+- Each decision is logged at info level with the probability and the outcome.
+
 ## Built-in Commands
 
 Telegram auto-registers PicoClaw's top-level bot commands at startup, including `/start`, `/help`, `/show`, `/list`, and `/use`.
